# Iterator — an M2 validation project (00 §33.2, 11.3).
#
# A walk over a class that `does iterable`: its `give next` method is the
# protocol the checker proves and both backends poll through the 12.3
# vtable. The program walks it twice — once widowed to say the turns, once
# gathered into a total — and then walks a plain list through the same
# `repeat for each` shape, with a `next round` inside (the continue
# statement rides every loop form). Deterministic: no stdin, no seed, no
# files, nothing asked.

class count down does iterable
  has left of type number
  can give next
    returns a number or nothing
    if (left of myself) is equal to 0
      gives back nothing
    set left of myself to (left of myself) - 1
    gives back (left of myself) + 1

# ----- the walk: one poll per turn, total gathered -------------------------

make walk equal to a new count down with left 3
make changing gathered equal to 0
repeat for each turn in walk
  say turn
  increase gathered by turn
say gathered

# ----- the same shape over a list, with a `next round` inside --------------

make parts equal to a list of 1, 2, 3, 4
make changing seen equal to 0
repeat for each part in parts
  if part is equal to 2
    next
  say part
  increase seen by 1
say seen
say "walked"
